    {
      "id": "revelation",
      "number": 6,
      "title": "The Revelation",
      "summary": "Committee and hearing papers fill an evidence board. Agent Fox points to the records.",
      "duration": 20,
      "authoredDuration": 18,
      "transition": "ink",
      "narration": "So how did any of this come out? In January 1975, the Senate created a special committee, chaired by Senator Frank Church. Its job was to find out whether America's intelligence agencies had done anything illegal, improper or unethical.",
