    {
      "id": "scene-l8nb63",
      "number": 7,
      "title": "The Hearing",
      "summary": "Painted cutaways: the archive where seven boxes were found, then the 1977 Senate hearing room and Kennedy's words.",
      "duration": 21,
      "authoredDuration": 21,
      "transition": "fade",
      "narration": "Then, in 1977, a CIA employee found seven boxes of MKUltra records at a retired records center. That August, senators questioned the CIA director at a joint hearing. Senator Edward Kennedy said the CIA had drugged American citizens without their knowledge or consent.",
